  "goodToKnow": "Die Mündung is the mouth of a river, where it flows into another river or the sea: die Elbmündung, die Rheinmündung (in the Netherlands). At the Deutsches Eck in Koblenz, the Mosel flows into the Rhine. It also means the muzzle of a gun. The verb münden in means to flow into, and figuratively to lead to: Die Debatte mündete in einen Streit. From der Mund (mouth). Plural: die Mündungen."
